From 6a87f26f8d143a739bc4b63ecadba4c3538798a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:42:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] perf(windows): read browser command lines natively
 instead of spawning powershell

Every browser action re-proves its binding three times (authorize, validate,
invoke), and each proof read the browser's command line twice through
PowerShell's Get-CimInstance, about 400 ms per read. Actions took 2.2-2.6 s.

Read it with NtQueryInformationProcess(ProcessCommandLineInformation) and keep
PowerShell only as a fallback for processes that can't be opened. Classification
also takes the exe name from the process instead of a Toolhelp snapshot of
every process. Revalidation drops from ~800 ms to ~3 ms; every check it makes
is unchanged.
